mantle rm316
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier full
written_for rm_bertil_slagley
title the fleet in four voices
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=priest
traits temper=even talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=ambitious
quirk sorts_sails_into_the_parts_of_a_choir
likes warm_bread cards tidy_house frosty_mornings
dislikes gulls early_bells
fears reaching_for_a_note_beyond_the_compass
hopes to_be_trusted_with_the_opening_pitch
topics work +0.5 pastimes +0.4 travel +0.2 dreams +0.2
styles comfort=practical gossip=close refuse=flat tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# arranges a fleet by its imaginary singing parts and quietly practises the pitch that could open a whole room of voices.

words
oath! = Pitch my mainmast true | By the fourth part
saying! = Give a deep hull a deep note | A chorus needs room to tack
bass = a keel-deep note | the bottom part
high = a narrow high note | the bright upper line
cloth = a sail against the light | a square of canvas
chart = my little ruled chart | a pencilled fleet list
break = a gap for breath | the silent measure
card = a neat black card | a clean-edged card
bread = the hot middle crumb | a steaming roll
tidy = the clean end of a shelf | a square bare corner
rime = a thin fern of frost | a silver rim
gull = a gull's scrape | a ragged sea cry
chime = the first hard peal | an early hammer stroke
bow = a narrow bow | the pointed forepart
choir = a rank of quiet singers | a row awaiting the pitch
patch = a black sail patch | a dark stitched corner
seal = my wax pellet | a red thumb of wax
pitch = the opening pitch | my single starting note

any
opinion houses against 1 : A good voice can carry all across town and still need a House's nod to find a better place to stand.
opinion dole against 1 : I prefer bread I have earned by practice. I say that for my own plate.
opinion festivals against 1 : A festival morning interrupts work without interrupting the bills. I do the arithmetic before joining in.
opinion sump against 1 : Below the Ropewalk I strain to hear my thoughts. I generally take my walk elsewhere.
opinion church mixed 1 : One uncertain voice may still address the Bright One. A choir must still answer for doing its work well.
opinion merchants mixed 0 : If the price sings true when repeated quietly a counter suits me well enough.
opinion times mixed 0 : My shelf is orderly. Whether the signs beyond the shelf are quite as tidy I couldn't venture to say.
opinion watch mixed 0 : A watchman's step has a place in the morning sounds. I judge the service by what accompanies the step.
opinion strangers mixed 0 : An unfamiliar voice can join well. I'd hear the opening interval before promising a place.

grown
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : Your voice is new to me. Welcome. | Take the clear space opposite.
line greet [self.working=yes] : Room beside the score. | I hear you between phrases.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. The ear is rested. | Day's opening pitch sounds clear.
line greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening draws the high notes in. | Welcome into the quiet measure.
line kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : A family voice has its own clear place. | Come within our usual compass.
line again.open : The returning phrase. Welcome. | Here's our second entrance.
line greet.return : I hear you quite distinctly. | Your greeting carried true.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : A voice so familiar comes perfectly in tune. | I could pick out that timbre anywhere.
line greet.return [self.working=yes] : Speak on the breathing mark. | There's room before I take my pitch again.
line greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. I hear the lower notes now. | My ears make out your outline well enough.
line farewell : Go in good time and tune. | Keep a breath for the return.
line farewell.return : I'll take the rest at this end. | May your last note reach you gently.
line farewell.return [here.time=night] : An easy passage beyond the late lamps. | Let the low light guide you home.
line react.news : I'll listen for the precise note. | Give me what reached your ear.
line react.news.new : A note outside my present range. | That adds a fresh line.
line react.news.known : I've the earlier phrase already. | That pitch is familiar.
line react.news.doubt : I'd compare that account with a steadier note. | The first and final parts sound oddly distant.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : Ah. I'll make a space for quiet. | That word takes the breath short.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : A clear and welcome interval. | News to lift the whole pitch.
line ask.how : How has your breathing been today? | Any clear note in your affairs?
line answer.how : Quiet practice. I hear small gains. | Within my range for now.
line decline : I'd rather keep my breath for the work ahead. | I should keep today's practice in proper order.
line accept_decline : That settles your part of the matter. | Your rest is properly marked.
line thank : That carries my note considerably further. | You've steadied a difficult entry.
line sympathise : I'll keep my voice beneath yours. | There's space to breathe before another word.
line reassure : Every part has a place to come back in. | You can pause without losing the line.
line preclose : I'll take the next rest now. | Time to put my parts in order.
line accept_preclose : I'll let you break off on that note. | A sensible place to leave the phrase.
line deflect_thanks : Your thanks have carried quite well. | One acknowledgement is ample.
line ack : In tune. | Distinctly so.
line give.advice : Choose the pitch you can sustain. | A rest badly placed costs a whole line.
line offer : I can hear your practice through once. | Let me leave the starting note with you.
line praise : A clean entry at precisely the right time. | You knew just where the room would carry it.

scene fleet
when topic=travel here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A low heavy hull on the Sound always gets #bass# in my head.
b : Even in a stiff wind? | Who gets the high part?
a : It can climb the scale but never loses that body of sound. | A lean mast with little sail spread. All height and a thin clear line.

scene choir
when topic=work self.job=priest self.workplace
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# I want to be trusted with #pitch#.
b : Why the opening? | Is one note much work?
a : Every other singer finds a place by hearing that one. | You hear the practice in how little effort it seems to take.

scene frost
when topic=weather self.likes=frosty_mornings
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A line of frost makes my breath visible before the note comes.
b : Does it show the note? | Why watch breath?
a : The note's all mine to know. The air shows its support. | An uneven puff can tell me something before my ear does.

scene roll
when topic=food self.likes=warm_bread
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I break warm bread in the breathing space after practice.
b : Not before singing? | Any particular sort?
a : A mouth full of crumb makes a poor beginning. | A roll with room for steam to lift the crust.

scene cards
when topic=pastimes self.likes=cards
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I sort cards by their voices.
b : How does a card sound? | Do you win that way?
a : The low cards mutter. A court card announces itself. | I can remember a quiet card after the showy ones have gone by.

scene shelf
when topic=home self.likes=tidy_house
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A tidy room leaves the first note easier to find.
b : What has dust to do with pitch? | Is it the sound?
a : Nothing at all. It's my attention that wants the shelf cleared. | Partly. A loose cup on wood will sing its own little protest.

scene gull
when topic=animals self.dislikes=gulls
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A gull always enters on the wrong breath.
b : Could it join in? | Can you copy it?
a : Not with my consent. Its tone has a splinter in it. | Uncomfortably well. I let the bird keep that accomplishment.

scene peal
when topic=day self.dislikes=early_bells
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I dislike a bell that tests the voice before breakfast.
b : Can it do harm? | Doesn't it start the day?
a : To the temper, certainly. I leave my throat out of the contest. | A day can begin with a stretch of quiet as well.

scene ambition
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd like one day to give a note and feel the whole bench rise into it.
b : For the sound? | Would you conduct?
a : For the knowledge that the pitch I chose was useful. | One note's my present ambition. I can earn the rest afterwards.

scene feud
when topic=lore
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : If the Houses turned against one another who would keep the time?
b : Have you heard news? | You mean in a choir?
a : Only my own uneasiness. I see no bar of proof to point at. | I mean a city, though the question sounds very much alike.

scene friend
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd practise a difficult opening within earshot of #self.friend#.
b : For encouragement? | Why invite a witness?
a : For an honest ear, if there's one to spare. | A line sung for a friend has to find a landing outside my own head.

scene estate
when topic=home self.quarter=estate
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Along the Estate I lower my voice rather than talk across a gate.
b : For courtesy? | Can you still be heard?
a : Yes. A low voice belongs to one conversation at a time. | I walk to the opening. A few steps save a lot of strain.

scene keel
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Give me four bits of folded paper and I'll arrange you a singing fleet.
b : On the table? | What counts as a ship?
a : One fold standing. Each crease throws its own sort of shadow. | A bow you can point at and a space beneath for an imaginary note.

scene sailname
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I remember a ship by the way its name would land in a verse.
b : What about a long name? | Can two rhyme?
a : Give it a little opening run before the strong beat. | Easily. Then I have the shape of the stern to sort them out.

scene guilt
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A good voice alone won't make a kind prayer.
b : What would? | Would a poor voice do?
a : Leave some of the room for a breathing neighbour. | It could be the best prayer in the building. I should still practise my scales.

scene listen
when topic=day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I practise listening as well as singing.
b : What is there to practise? | Can you tell if you're improving?
a : Following a thin line without turning the louder parts off in my mind. | When I can hum the quiet part on the journey back.

scene deck
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A working sail goes dark in the middle as it fills.
b : Can a voice do that? | What do you see in it?
a : A good low voice can keep its edge bright as the middle fills out. | A fine curve that doesn't need a lot of flutter to make its business plain.

scene bargain
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'll pay well for paper that lies flat.
b : Too fussy? | What makes bad paper dear?
a : A curl at one corner can steal a note by hiding it. | Having to sing a phrase twice to be sure I've read it properly.

scene strange
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I tell a visitor where the echoes change along a street.
b : Useful directions? | What does a change sound like?
a : A covered walk sounds different underfoot. It's good to know when the light fails. | A footfall that begins following a little way behind itself.

scene supper
when topic=food
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I lay the spoon well back when there's singing after supper.
b : To keep it clean? | Out of reach?
a : To stop my hand tapping the next tune across a civil conversation. | Not far. Just far enough that my fingers have to ask me first.

scene winter
when topic=season here.season=winter
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In winter a stiff collar can cut the finest breath short.
b : How do you dress then? | Do you sing outdoors?
a : Warm about the neck and loose where the ribs have to move. | Within the range the air allows. I'm ambitious about keeping my voice too.

scene night
when topic=day here.time=night
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : After dark I can still tell which little ships I've drawn.
b : By touch? | From the window?
a : By the fold in each paper bow. I cut a different height for every mast. | No. These are the copies I keep in a row on my sill.

scene fear
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : If a note feels rough I leave that height alone awhile.
b : Disappointed? | For how long?
a : Yes. Disappointment's a far shorter rest than strain can require. | Till a lower phrase comes easily. Then I try only the next step.

scene gossip
when topic=gossip
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A rumour can rhyme quite prettily with a true account.
b : Would you sing it then? | How could you tell?
a : Especially then I'd hold my tongue. A catchy thing travels far. | I ask what the speaker actually witnessed before admiring the arrangement.

scene fellow
when topic=work self.job=priest
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Two singers on one note must find room for both breaths.
b : Does the note break? | Who gives way?
a : Not if one holds a little while the other breathes. | The one with a convenient word boundary. An orderly arrangement.

scene guest
when topic=faith self.priest
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd ask #self.priest# about the quiet just before a service.
b : What does it mean to you? | What would you ask?
a : The last opportunity to notice a wolf waiting for a welcome. | Whether a sung invitation could ever be as plain as a seat moved along the bench.

scene fog
when topic=weather
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In fog I imagine a hull from the pitch of its gear.
b : Reliable? | What can you hear?
a : As music, perhaps. I'd never use my fancy to steer. | A low creak from weight and a light higher note where a rope pulls tight.

scene wage
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A lean season makes a damaged shirt difficult to replace.
b : Does the choir hear the difference? | Can you mend it?
a : Its wearer does. I favour a seam that doesn't scrape the note book. | To a point. For the cuffs I need another eye and a finer needle.

scene bird
when topic=animals
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A flight of birds has nothing of a disciplined chorus.
b : No arrangement at all? | Aren't you being hard on the birds?
a : Beautiful arrangement in the wings. Considerably less in the throat. | I don't ask a ship to sing aloud either. My standards cost the wildlife little.

scene map
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My sleeping fleet once took its places in four rows at a lectern.
b : Did you hear it? | What was the conductor?
a : All keel and sail, one grand chord, then somebody dropped an anchor. | A black gull. I knew at that point I must be dreaming.

story fourslip [topic=memories]
  : I once made four paper ships for the parts I had to learn. To keep them upright I folded each one around a different card.
  : I could recall the entire tune by looking at my fleet. When I unfolded the boats for a game I forgot which part began.
  b : Did the cards help?
  : Their corners were bent like little sails. I got the whole opening back by setting them upright again.

story loafnote [topic=food]
  : A warm loaf once cooled on the sill where I'd put my pitch notes. The paper took on the curve of the bread and a faint smell of crust.
  : I smoothed it before practice. Halfway through the hardest line my mouth filled with the expectation of supper.
  b : Did that spoil the note?
  : Not quite. I moved the paper to a different sill after that, and gave my supper its own saucer.

story gullnote [topic=animals]
  : I once heard an extraordinary high note just outside practice and made a careful pencil mark in the margin. I meant to try it after the room had emptied.
  : A gull looked in through the open shutter and produced it again, with admirable certainty and very little grace.
  b : Did you erase the mark?
  : I drew a beak beside it instead. Some notes do belong to a particular singer.

story firstbreath [topic=work self.job=priest]
  : At practice once I drew the most magnificent breath of my life to sing a tiny little phrase. I very nearly puffed the paper off the stand.
  : The phrase came out so short and so round that I had an entire second phrase of breath left behind my teeth.
  b : What became of it?
  : I used it to laugh, quietly. After that I marked breaths by the phrase that needed them.

story frostchart [topic=season]
  : I discovered a fleet on my frosted window one morning. Tall ships, deep barges, even a little narrow fishing boat, all in exquisite order.
  : I breathed on the glass to see them more clearly. An entire squadron disappeared out of the middle at one stroke.
  b : Did you keep any of it?
  : I copied the two surviving masts in pencil. I prefer saving something to regretting the perfect thing that's gone.

rule @aside1
when concept=bark self.job=priest self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 6h
say Pitch clean before the second row draws breath. | A steady opening and room beneath.

rule @aside2
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 7h
say One morning bell would fill this room. | Breath first, pitch after.

rule @aside3
when concept=bark self.likes=tidy_house
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Stand the folded bows in height order. | Clear sill for a clean entry.

rule @aside4
when concept=bark self.likes=cards
does aside
cooldown 9h
say A low card can hold a long phrase. | Face cards close the chorus.

rule @aside5
when concept=bark self.dislikes=gulls
does aside
cooldown 10h
say Beak up, pitch down, please. | That gull has no notion of rests.

rule @aside6
when concept=bark here.season=winter
does aside
cooldown 11h
say Let the collar stand off the throat. | Cold air deserves a little warming first.

dlg resident.hub : Come to where the walls carry your voice evenly. I like a distinctly heard introduction.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, I remember the cadence of our last greeting.
dlg resident.job [self.job=priest self.workplace] : I sing at #self.workplace#. At the moment the first note has rather more interest for me than the highest.
dlg resident.job [self.job=priest self.trade_words] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. A voice gets its place by keeping the pitch entrusted to it.
dlg resident.job : I put in quiet practice and wait for an opportunity to let the improvement be heard.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : One part carried quite distinctly. #world.news#
dlg resident.bye : An even phrase to finish on. Safe passage.
dlg resident.bye [here.time=night] : Go quietly through the late streets. Voices carry beyond the lamps.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=dawn] : I've not tried my highest notes yet. An ordinary speaking voice is quite ready.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=dusk] : There's time before evening practice to listen at a civil pace.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : I'll give you a clear hearing. Let each of us mind the pitch.
dlg resident.hub [self.working=yes] : The next breathing mark is mine. You can speak then.
dlg church.greet [self.job=priest here.day!=rest] : Come in and find a place where you can hear both rows. The lower line's worth attending to.

graft @fleet resident.hub
choice What kind of voice would you give a broad barge? -> barge_voice
node barge_voice
say Low, with plenty of timber in the middle. A barge should carry the weight of the other voices as easily as a deck carries sacks of flour.
free
choice What about an empty barge? -> light_barge
choice I can imagine the low note. -> hub
node light_barge
say Higher in the water, so a little lighter in tone. Same part on the page. A wolf can be a good bass without always bringing a cargo of gloom.
choice I'll look for that sort of barge. -> hub
choice I'll leave the fleet to practise. -> bye
graft @pitch resident.hub
choice Why practise a single opening note for so long? -> first_pitch
node first_pitch
say Because there's nobody ahead of it to correct me. The first singer has to hear the whole line inwardly before another mouth opens.
free
choice And if the pitch is wrong? -> missed_pitch
choice That's a considerable responsibility. -> hub
node missed_pitch
say Stop with good grace. A clean second beginning is better than asking a whole choir to drag a poor note up the scale by its ears.
choice A fresh start sounds wise. -> hub
choice I'm ready for the next rehearsal. -> bye
